.TH STAT 2P "August 1, 1992"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
stat, fstat \- (POSIX version) get file status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <sys/types.h>
#include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.ft B
int stat(const char *\fIpath\fP, struct stat *\fIbuf\fP);
.PP
.ft B
int fstat(int \fIfd\fP, struct stat *\fIbuf\fP);
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The information in this specification applies
only to POSIX applications.
.PP
This is the POSIX specification for \fIstat\fR.
For the BSD specification, see \fIstat\fR(2).
.PP
The
.IR stat 
function obtains information about the file
whose name is given by \fIpath\fP.
Read, write or execute
permission of the named file is not required, but all directories
listed in the pathname leading to the file must be searchable.
.PP
The
.IR fstat 
function obtains the same information about an open file
referenced by the file descriptor \fIfd\fP.
.PP
The \fIbuf\fP argument is a pointer to a \fIstat\fP
structure, into which information is placed concerning the file.
The \fIstat\fP structure is defined in the header
.I <sys/stat.h>
and includes the following members:
.IP
.PP
.RS
.TP 35
\fBMember Type	Member Name\fP
\fBDescription\fP
.TP 35
\fImode_t		st_mode\fP
File mode.
.TP 35
\fIino_t		st_ino\fP
File's inode number.
.TP 35
\fIdev_t		st_dev\fP
ID of device containing the file.
.TP 35
\fInlink_t		st_nlink\fP
Number of links to the file.
.TP 35
\fIuid_t		st_uid\fP
User ID of the file's owner.
.TP 35
\fIgid_t		st_gid\fP
Group ID of the file's group.
.TP 35
\fIoff_t		st_size\fP
File size in bytes.
.TP 35
\fItime_t		st_atime\fP
Time of last access.
.TP 35
\fItime_t		st_mtime\fP
Time of last data modification.
.TP 35
\fItime_t		st_ctime\fP
Time of last file status change.
.RE
.IP
.PP
The values of the time-related fields are given in seconds since
the Epoch.
.PP
The header
.I <sys/stat.h>
also defines the following macros which can be used
to test whether a file is of the specified type.
The value \fIm\fP supplied to the macros must be the the value of
the \fIst_mode\fP member of a \fIstat\fP structure.
Each macro evaluates to a nonzero value if the test is true, and zero if
the test is false.
.IP
.PP
.RS
.TP 15
S_ISDIR(\fIm\fP)
Test macro for a directory.
.TP 15
S_ISCHR(\fIm\fP)
Test macro for a character special file.
.TP 15
S_ISBLK(\fIm\fP)
Test macro for a block special file.
.TP 15
S_ISREG(\fIm\fP)
Test macro for a regular file.
.TP 15
S_ISFIFO(\fIm\fP)
Test macro for a FIFO.
.RE
.IP
.PP
Furthermore,
.I <sys/stat.h>
includes the following masks and bits which can
used to encode or decode the file modes portion of values of type
\fImode_t\fP, such as the \fIst_mode\fP member of the \fIstat\fP structure.
.IP
.PP
.RS
.TP 15
S_IRWXU
Read, write, execute (if a non-directory), or search
(if a directory) \*(lqowner\*(rq permissions mask.
.RS 17
.TP 15
S_IRUSR
\*(lqOwner\*(rq read permission bit.
.TP 15
S_IWUSR
\*(lqOwner\*(rq write permission bit.
.TP 15
S_IXUSR
\*(lqOwner\*(rq execute (if a non-directory) or search (if a directory)
permission bit.
.RE
.
.TP 15
S_IRWXG
Read, write, execute (if a non-directory), or search
(if a directory) \*(lqgroup\*(rq permissions mask.
.RS 17
.TP 15
S_IRGRP
\*(lqGroup\*(rq read permission bit.
.TP 15
S_IWGRP
\*(lqGroup\*(rq write permission bit.
.TP 15
S_IXGRP
\*(lqGroup\*(rq execute (if a non-directory) or search (if a directory)
permission bit.
.RE
.
.TP 15
S_IRWXO
Read, write, execute (if a non-directory), or search
(if a directory) \*(lqother\*(rq permissions mask.
.RS 17
.TP 15
S_IROTH
\*(lqOther\*(rq read permission bit.
.TP 15
S_IWOTH
\*(lqOther\*(rq write permission bit.
.TP 15
S_IXOTH
\*(lqOther\*(rq execute (if a non-directory) or search (if a directory)
permission bit.
.RE
.
.TP 15
S_ISUID
Set-user-id bit.
The effective user ID of the process is set to that of the file's owner
when the file is executed.
On a regular file, this bit is cleared on any write.
.
.TP 15
S_ISGID
Set-group-id bit.
The effective group ID of the process is set to that of the file's group
when the file is executed.
On a regular file, this bit is cleared on any write.
.RE
.IP
.PP
The S_IRWXU mask is the bitwise inclusive OR of the S_IRUSR, S_IWUSR and
S_IXUSR bits.
.PP
The S_IRWXG mask is the bitwise inclusive OR of the S_IRGRP, S_IWGRP and
S_IXGRP bits.
.PP
The S_IRWXO mask is the bitwise inclusive OR of the S_IROTH, S_IWOTH and
S_IXOTH bits.
.PP
Both
.IR stat 
and
.IR fstat 
functions update any time-related fields of the named file before writing into the \fIstat\fP structure.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Upon successful completion a value of zero is returned.
Otherwise, a value of \-1 is returned and \fIerrno\fP
is set to indicate the error.
.SH "ERRORS"
If any of the following conditions occurs,
.IR stat 
returns \-1 and sets \fIerrno\fP to the corresponding value:
.TP 15
[EACCES]
Search permission is denied for a component of the path prefix.
.TP 15
[EFAULT]
Either \fIpath\fP or \fIbuf\fP points outside the process's allocated
address space.
.TP 15
[EINVAL]
The pathname contains a character with the high-order bit set.
.TP 15
[EIO]
An I/O error occurred while reading from or writing to the file system.
.TP 15
[ELOOP]
Too many symbolic links were encountered in translating the pathname.
.TP 15
[ENAMETOOLONG]
A component of \fIpath\fP exceeds {NAME_MAX} (see <limits.h>)
characters,
or the entire pathname exceeds {PATH_MAX} (see <limits.h>)
characters.
.TP 15
[ENOENT]
The named file does not exist.
.TP 15
[ENOENT]
The \fIpath\fP argument points to an empty string.
.TP 15
[ENOTDIR]
A component of the path prefix is not a directory.
.PP
.PP
If any of the following conditions occurs,
.IR fstat 
returns \-1 and sets \fIerrno\fP to the corresponding value:
.TP 15
[EBADF]
The \fIfd\fP argument
is not a valid open file descriptor.
.TP 15
[EFAULT]
The \fIbuf\fP argument points outside the process's allocated
address space.
.TP 15
[EIO]
An I/O error occurred while reading from or writing to the file system.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
chmod(2P),
chown(2P),
creat(2P),
dup(2P),
fcntl(2P),
open(2P),
pipe(2P),
stat(2)
